  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "f0346bfa-9574-44ae-b46e-d4cf84a0a361",
    "name": "Reschedule appointment",
    "description": "Demonstrates patient-initiated rescheduling of an active appointment and the billing outcome for both the original and replacement appointments.\n\n**Prerequisites**\n\n- The Scheduling and Billing services and their required infrastructure are running.\n    \n- The selected environment contains `scheduling_url` and `billing_url`.\n    \n- An active appointment eligible for rescheduling exists.\n    \n- The requested new slot is available, fits within the doctor’s working hours, and does not overlap an unavailable period.\n    \n- For a paid-appointment scenario, keep Stripe webhook forwarding active.\n    \n\n**Request order**\n\n1. **Get the latest active appointment** — retrieve the original appointment and save its ID as `appointmentIdOld`.\n    \n2. **Reschedule appointment** — request a new date and time with `cancelInitiator` set to `PATIENT`; save the returned appointment ID as `appointmentIdNew`.\n    \n3. **Get invoice status Old** — inspect billing for the original appointment.\n    \n4. **Get invoice status New** — inspect billing for the replacement appointment.\n    \n\nThe scripts store `appointmentIdOld` and `appointmentIdNew` as collection variables.\n\nBilling processes appointment events asynchronously. Allow time for processing before checking the resulting invoice states.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "_exporter_id": "57059525"
  },
  "item": [
